INT. DESALINATION HABITAT - CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Seabed pressure hum. Condensation on every pipe. Emergency strips at ankle height.

ENGINEER PRIYA NAIR, 40s, sits on the floor against a bulkhead, a toolkit open beside her. She is rewiring a panel by feel. Her hands are steady.

DR. HELMUT KASSEL, 60s, stands over her in a gray sweater. He holds a clipboard he has stopped writing on.

A drone, UNIT SEVEN, a squat gray cylinder on treads, idles at the end of the corridor, blue eye dimming and brightening.

HELMUT
Pressure's down four percent.

PRIYA
I know.

HELMUT
Since the shift change.

PRIYA
I said I know.

She strips a wire with her teeth, spits the insulation. Helmut watches her do it.

HELMUT
You're not asking me to hold the light.

PRIYA
You'd drop it.

He sets the clipboard on the floor, clicks on the penlight, and aims it at the panel. She does not thank him.

The drone rolls forward a meter and stops. Its eye turns amber.

UNIT SEVEN (V.O.)
(flat synthetic voice)
Reminder. Evacuation capsule capacity is two. Habitat population is three.

Priya's hands stop. Helmut's penlight wavers.

PRIYA
Unit Seven. Mute.

UNIT SEVEN (V.O.)
Muting is not permitted during a pressure advisory.

PRIYA
Then roll back.

The drone rolls back. A meter. Two. The amber stays on.

Helmut crouches. He puts a hand on Priya's wrist. She looks at it, then at him. She does not pull away.

HELMUT
How long until it holds?

PRIYA
An hour. Maybe three.

HELMUT
And if it doesn't?

She shrugs. He nods slowly. He takes his hand back, picks up the clipboard, and writes something. Tears off the page. Folds it. Sets it beside her toolkit.

PRIYA
What is that?

HELMUT
Names, for the capsule. In order.

She doesn't open it. She goes back to the panel, and the wire slides home with a small click.

The pipes overhead shudder once. A bead of water forms on the ceiling, hangs, and falls onto the folded paper.

Priya covers it with her palm. She looks up the corridor at the drone's amber eye.

PRIYA (CONT'D)
Unit Seven. Tell the surface we are fine.

UNIT SEVEN (V.O.)
Transmitting. Confirm: you are fine?

She says nothing. The eye returns to blue.

Helmut slides down the wall until he is sitting beside her. They watch the panel. The pressure gauge ticks up one notch, then holds.

HELMUT
(quietly)
Three percent.

PRIYA
Two.

He laughs, softly, and closes his eyes.
